#: ../../source/api/stability.md:1 17214666ac414ede90bc6a46b2455dff
msgid "API Stability Policy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api/stability.md:3 302af3debf434458835641b6d51ee673
msgid ""
"`findfmt` follows [Semantic Versioning "
"2.0.0](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html). This page defines what the "
"public Python API is, what stays compatible within the 1.x line, and how "
"changes are caught before release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api/stability.md:7 d32b770f0e51441fbb822cb3be0fae82
msgid "1. What Is Public"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api/stability.md:9 56ca9da369594f05bd143a868c403f06
msgid ""
"The public API is every name listed in the `__all__` of the `findfmt` "
"package and its submodules. Everything else is internal and may change in"
" any release:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api/stability.md:12 2956e1ab5ec74730b4ecf856dbd1a11f
msgid "names that start with an underscore, or are not listed in `__all__`;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api/stability.md:13 f4ce700d357647d6b3dccff25acc1c51
msgid "the `tools/` and `tests/` directories."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api/stability.md:15 3f200e09a4554ab298c1f7585973482e
msgid ""
"Command-line options, configuration keys, environment variables, and "
"[exit codes](../cli/index.md) are covered by the same compatibility "
"promise as the Python API."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api/stability.md:18 f24cc5b3bdd44af6935862c4e3e38fd1
msgid "2. Compatibility Within 1.x"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api/stability.md:20 549d302d497347ebb0cdda17737b4515
msgid "Within the 1.x line:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api/stability.md:22 c7f5509df3fb400e93f1f68b578e687d
msgid "Public names are not removed or renamed without a deprecation period."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api/stability.md:23 99208c8edae64c3b9b9662f429c2e137
msgid ""
"Existing calls keep working: new parameters are optional, and are added "
"at the end or as keyword-only parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api/stability.md:25 7d225474d9204ce6a3b4ea1fd7e9de26
msgid ""
"Enum members keep their names and values, and comparisons with those "
"values keep working."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api/stability.md:26 b65d5477430541199b16faa7db9f5dae
msgid "Exception classes keep their place in the `FindFmtError` hierarchy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api/stability.md:28 cf8e386591e8474bac84cb621e29f884
msgid "2.1. Pass Arguments by Keyword"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api/stability.md:30 02947aa8ddd3465c9af6c5a18e31a22a
msgid ""
"Some public callables take many parameters, and their positional order is"
" not guaranteed. Pass arguments to these by keyword:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api/stability.md:33 65fe27b785d24d9aa666c9488bdc67c8
msgid ""
"**`TraversalConfig`**: 1.0.2 inserted `csv_safe` in the middle of its "
"fields."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api/stability.md:34 e8277ff421ba42b991c6db81d0a89f58
msgid ""
"**CLI command callbacks** such as `findfmt.cli.findfmt`: Click always "
"calls them by keyword, and 1.1 inserted `exit_status` in the middle of "
"the signature."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api/stability.md:37 46473f2f6c154585a7709f555d6e3d2a
msgid ""
"Version 2.0 will make these parameters keyword-only "
"([#504](https://github.com/bdperkin/findfmt/issues/504))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api/stability.md:40 cd46eb47a6f644ec9073c8e820346c58
msgid "2.2. Documented Exceptions in 1.1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api/stability.md:42 b1abbc0a78074268a2c79abbe1479522
msgid ""
"1.1 changes two things that 1.0.x users can notice. Both are listed as "
"breaking changes in the changelog and explained in [Upgrading to findfmt "
"1.1](../guides/upgrading.md):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api/stability.md:45 5f618861c38b422397600638c54ba62c
msgid "Python 3.10 is no longer supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api/stability.md:46 edf5ad60e9204cc0becc6768fbce3e75
msgid ""
"`SortKey` and `OutputFormat` are `enum.StrEnum` subclasses, so `str()` "
"and f-strings return a member's value. Member names, values, and "
"comparisons are unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api/stability.md:49 e8f94c0a56864f1aa642b980fbe02a94
msgid "3. How Changes Are Caught"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api/stability.md:51 3ef51d79459442b092a9225bab4cf6b2
msgid ""
"`tools/api_surface.py` records every public name with its kind and, where"
" meaningful, its signature, class members, or enum values. The committed "
"snapshot `tests/unit/api_surface.json` pins that surface, and "
"`tests/unit/test_api_surface.py` fails when the API changes. The failure "
"lists the added, removed, and changed names."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api/stability.md:56 86851bfd5518453da557d7e9437c254f
msgid "To make an intentional API change:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api/stability.md:58 5ba14f4add424f9b8fab5cd50735e371
msgid "Regenerate the snapshot with `uv run python tools/api_surface.py --write`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api/stability.md:59 f614e37b955446d3b82f8984ff89a1d1
msgid ""
"Record the change in `CHANGELOG.md`, and add it to the upgrade notes if "
"it can break callers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api/stability.md:61 099c52a4581f469a9b9677f5a810b2ab
msgid "4. API Changes in 1.1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api/stability.md:63 2aaf2f82b4f848949cea8ea6d8c8a451
msgid ""
"Compared with 1.0.0, 1.1 removes no public names and adds 20, including "
"helpers for CSV formula-injection safety, `--exit-status`, atomic output "
"files, and terminal cell widths. Signature changes add only optional or "
"keyword-only parameters, apart from the positional-order cases in §2.1. "
"Compared with the latest 1.0.x release (1.0.2), 1.1 adds 2 names (both "
"for `--exit-status`) and changes the two `StrEnum` classes, the CLI "
"command callbacks, and `execute_findfmt` (a new keyword-only "
"`exit_status` parameter)."
msgstr ""
